The class `FutureDisposable` is a lightweight wrapper around `Future` with simple state checks and a single cancel operation. It contains no computationally intensive logic or algorithmic complexity that would benefit from microbenchmarking. Measuring its performance with JMH would provide limited insight, as the overhead is dominated by the underlying `Future` implementation and JVM infrastructure rather than the wrapper itself. Therefore, generating a JMH benchmark is unnecessary.